# agent-ops-kit — one env file for the whole stack.
#   cp .env.example .env   (or just `make init`, which also generates the secrets)
# Secrets are read by docker compose, scripts/hermes-install.sh and scripts/doctor.sh.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Network ---
# Keep every service on 127.0.0.1 (this machine only) — the safe default and the
# canonical setup. To reach a service from a remote worker (the Windows VM), do
# NOT change these binds: publish the loopback port to your tailnet with
# Tailscale Serve instead — `make windows-vm-network` (forwards :8317 and :8000,
# tailnet-only, Docker stays on loopback). The host's own Hermes and `make doctor`
# probe 127.0.0.1, so a non-loopback bind here would break them and the forward.
#
# CLIProxyAPI (ChatGPT proxy) — the only surface a Windows VM worker needs.
CLIPROXY_BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1
# Honcho memory API. Runs with auth disabled — keep it loopback-only. Share it
# with the worker (opt-in) via Tailscale Serve, not by binding it to a routable IP.
HONCHO_BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1
# claude-max-proxy (host systemd service). It spawns Claude Code sessions with
# host access, so keep it loopback. If you set a non-loopback address you MUST
# also set CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_API_KEY below — the proxy refuses to start otherwise.
CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_BIND=127.0.0.1
# Where your repositories live. Hermes' terminal starts here and so does every
# Claude Code session the proxy spawns (its systemd WorkingDirectory).
REPOS_DIR=/opt/repos

# ------------------------------------------------- ChatGPT / Codex proxy ---
# CLIProxyAPI turns your ChatGPT subscription (Codex OAuth) into an
# OpenAI-compatible API on :8317. Log in once with `make auth-codex`.
CLIPROXY_PORT=8317
# Client key every consumer sends (Hermes, Honcho, Windows worker). `make init`
# fills these two in with random values when empty.
CLIPROXY_API_KEY=
CLIPROXY_MANAGEMENT_KEY=
# CLIPROXY_IMAGE=eceasy/cli-proxy-api:latest

# ------------------------------------------------------ Claude Max proxy ---
# claude-max-api-proxy turns your Claude Max subscription into an
# OpenAI-compatible API on :3456. Hermes sends coding work here. It runs ON
# THE HOST as a systemd user service (make claude-proxy-install), not in
# Docker: the Claude Code sessions it spawns then see your repos, toolchains
# (go, node, uv, ...), docker and gh exactly as you do, and survive rebuilds.
CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_PORT=3456
# Bearer secret required on the proxy's /v1/* and admin/ops surfaces. `make init`
# fills it with a random value when empty. Hermes (delegation), `make models`
# and `make doctor` send it automatically. The proxy REFUSES to start on a
# non-loopback CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_BIND unless this is set. Leave the default
# loopback bind and this is optional (loopback accepts any/no key).
CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_API_KEY=
# When you deliberately bind the proxy off-loopback, also list the Host headers
# it should accept (comma-separated host[:port]) to block DNS-rebinding, and any
# browser Origins allowed to call it. Empty = loopback only (the safe default).
# CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# Long-lived OAuth token (about a year). `make auth-claude-proxy` runs the login
# and stores it here. Until it is set the service idles instead of serving.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Sources are vendored in this repo (vendor/claude-max-api-proxy, pinned in its
# UPSTREAM file) and built with npm by `make claude-proxy-install`.
# `make claude-proxy-update` refreshes them from upstream when it is reachable
# and keeps the vendored copy when it is not. Override the source only if you
# maintain a fork.
# CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_DIR=./vendor/claude-max-api-proxy
# CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_REPO=https://github.com/mattschwen/claude-max-api-proxy.git
# CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_REF=main
# Extended-thinking budget applied when a client sends none: off|low|medium|high|xhigh|max
DEFAULT_THINKING_BUDGET=medium
# Claude Code sessions the proxy runs at the same time (Hermes subagents).
# Each one is a full CLI session plus whatever it spawns (builds, tests):
# budget ~1 core and ~4 GB each, and all of them share the Claude Max 5-hour
# window. Extra requests queue, they do not fail. Size the three limits below
# together: CPUS ~ 1.3 x sessions, MEM ~ 4G x sessions.
#   laptop / 4-core VM ....... 2 sessions, CPUS=3,  MEM_LIMIT=8G
#   8-core / 32 GB ........... 3 sessions, CPUS=4,  MEM_LIMIT=12G   (defaults)
#   16-core / 128 GB shared .. 6 sessions, CPUS=8,  MEM_LIMIT=24G
CLAUDE_PROXY_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS=3
# systemd cgroup limits for the proxy AND every Claude Code session/tool it
# spawns (CPUQuota, MemoryMax, TasksMax). This is what keeps a runaway session
# from freezing the host. Fractions are fine (2.5). Memory takes K/M/G.
CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_CPUS=4
CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_MEM_LIMIT=12G
CLAUDE_MAX_PROXY_TASKS_MAX=4096
# Restart the proxy after N hours of uptime, once no request is active or
# queued, so leaked CLI subprocesses and stale OAuth state are cleared.
# systemd brings it straight back. Empty or 0 disables.
CLAUDE_PROXY_MAX_UPTIME_HOURS=12

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Honcho ---
# Self-hosted Honcho (API + deriver + Postgres/pgvector + Redis).
HONCHO_PORT=8000
# Postgres password for honcho-db. `make init` generates it. Postgres only
# applies it when the data volume is first created (docs/troubleshooting.md).
HONCHO_DB_PASSWORD=
# Model Honcho's reasoning layer uses. Routed through CLIProxyAPI, so this must
# be a model your ChatGPT subscription exposes. Check with `make models`.
# The deriver makes many small calls per chat turn; a mid tier (Terra-class)
# is plenty here and spares the ChatGPT quota for the orchestrator.
HONCHO_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra
# Local embedding model served by Ollama (no API key). Dimensions must match
# the model: nomic-embed-text=768 (8k context, 274 MB, the default),
# bge-m3=1024 (8k context, multilingual, 1.2 GB), mxbai-embed-large=1024
# (512-token context: truncates Honcho's longer documents, not recommended).
# Honcho creates its vector columns at 1536; the kit's honcho-api entrypoint
# resizes them to this value on an EMPTY database. Changing it later = make clean.
HONCHO_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
HONCHO_EMBED_DIMENSIONS=768
# json_schema (default) or json_object — switch if the deriver logs
# "response_format" errors from the proxy.
HONCHO_STRUCTURED_OUTPUT_MODE=json_schema
HONCHO_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Identity inside Honcho. HONCHO_PEER_NAME is the peer that represents YOU:
# Honcho builds its model of the user under this name and every profile and
# the Windows worker read it, so they share what they learn about you. Any
# short id works (`me`, `norkz`). Set it before the first `make hermes-install`;
# changing it later starts a new peer with empty memory. HONCHO_WORKSPACE
# scopes all peers and sessions; one workspace per operator.
HONCHO_PEER_NAME=me
HONCHO_WORKSPACE=agent-ops
# OLLAMA_CPUS=2.0
# OLLAMA_MEM_LIMIT=3g
# OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=24h
# Local OpenAI-compatible endpoint the Hermes HOST reaches (model-router plugin
# private/aux work + fallback tail). Ollama in compose is loopback-only inside
# Docker; publish it to the host (or run a host Ollama) before private routing
# goes live — see docs/model-routing.md.
OLLAMA_PORT=11434
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# Private Honcho for #private turns (docs/model-routing.md, "Private Honcho
# route"). Validator only: Hermes has no per-turn memory route yet, so marked
# turns are refused for private memory. Reasoning and embeddings must be a local
# Ollama (never CLIProxyAPI/claude-max-proxy); the API must be a separate local
# Honcho, not the public one on HONCHO_PORT.
# PRIVATE_HONCHO_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8100
# PRIVATE_HONCHO_WORKSPACE=agent-ops-private
# PRIVATE_HONCHO_REASONING_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# PRIVATE_HONCHO_MODEL=qwen3.5:27b
# PRIVATE_HONCHO_EMBED_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# Local model roles, all on OLLAMA_BASE_URL (pulled CHAT models with tool
# support; check with `make local-models`). docs/model-routing.md, Local model roles.
#   routine  ordinary private turns and local-only fallback work
#   fallback tried once when a role model fails; last native fallback hop
#   agent    difficult private turns, private coding, native fallback agent
OLLAMA_ROUTINE_MODEL=qwen3.5:27b
OLLAMA_FALLBACK_MODEL=qwen3.6:27b
OLLAMA_AGENT_MODEL=qwen3.8:27b

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Hermes ---
# Primary model for the orchestrator (ChatGPT subscription via CLIProxyAPI).
# Use an id from `make models`. In the GPT-5.6 line `gpt-5.6` is OpenAI's
# alias for `gpt-5.6-sol` (flagship); `gpt-5.6-luna` is the fastest/lowest-cost
# tier and the routine floor complexity routing degrades to.
HERMES_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# Model for delegated coding subagents (Claude Max via claude-max-proxy).
# `opus`, `sonnet`, `haiku`, `default`, or an exact id from `make models`
# (for example the Fable id your account exposes).
HERMES_CODING_MODEL=opus

# --- model-router plugin (task routing + fail-closed privacy) --------------
# Task-scoped routing classifies the CURRENT user task only (never history or
# tool output) and rewrites model + reasoning effort within the family:
#   orchestrator  status/lookup->luna(low)   ordinary work->luna(medium)
#                 ambiguous/planning->terra   hard work->sol
#                 gpt-6-astra ONLY with a leading standalone #max/#astra line
#   coding        opus (default)              hard engineering->fable
# A leading standalone #opus/#fable line forces that coding model for the
# request (overrides complexity, effort left to the coding proxy). It is honored
# only on the coding seam; on the orchestrator seam it is refused, not faked with
# a GPT alias, and privacy always takes precedence over it.
# It only rewrites models it manages and degrades to an available tier; the
# automatic ceiling is sol (never astra without explicit authorization).
MODEL_ROUTER_COMPLEXITY=true
# Per-task reasoning-effort rewrite for managed orchestrator requests (never
# raised above the configured agent.reasoning_effort ceiling). Explicit false
# disables the effort rewrite while keeping model routing.
MODEL_ROUTER_EFFORT=true
# Astra policy: task (default) | always (legacy: any managed max-tier request
# allowed) | never (hard off). Explicit values are preserved by --force.
# MODEL_ROUTER_ASTRA=task
# Seconds a session's current-task state (continuation retention + per-task
# Astra authorization) stays live without a substantive follow-up.
# MODEL_ROUTER_TASK_TTL=1800
# Specialist router: when true, the orchestrator's turn gets a
# deterministic note naming the book-backed profiles the current task needs
# (0-6, MODEL_ROUTER_SPECIALIST_MAX). Private tasks never route to cloud-backed
# profiles. Verified attachment text can add deterministic domain signals before
# the final cap. Dry-run first: TASK="..." make specialist-route.
# MODEL_ROUTER_SPECIALIST_CLASSIFIER=cliproxy: for a public task with no or only
# weak keyword matches, or with verified attachments, CLIProxyAPI
# (gpt-5.6-terra, medium reasoning)
# reads the typed task plus the attached documents (PDF/DOCX text extracted
# locally). The final combined route is capped at six profiles. The classifier
# may add at most two non-high-risk profiles. #privacy/#private turns never
# reach either classifier; a timeout adds nothing (TIMEOUT seconds total, max 25).
# Presence-aware: a key set here wins (false stays false); a key left out keeps
# the value already in ~/.hermes/config.yaml on `hermes-install.sh --force`.
# See docs/specialist-routing.md.
MODEL_ROUTER_SPECIALISTS=true
MODEL_ROUTER_SPECIALIST_MAX=6
MODEL_ROUTER_SPECIALIST_REQUIRE_READY=false
MODEL_ROUTER_SPECIALIST_CLASSIFIER=cliproxy
MODEL_ROUTER_SPECIALIST_CLASSIFIER_TIMEOUT=25
MODEL_ROUTER_SPECIALIST_PROFILES=all
# Privacy routing is fail-closed and per request: a turn where you type
# #privacy or #private never reaches a cloud provider — it goes to local Ollama
# or is refused. #local is inert; the next unmarked turn is public, with earlier
# private turns withheld from it. Leave this on: with false, privacy protection
# is disabled.
MODEL_ROUTER_PRIVACY=false

# Auxiliary routing:
# - Session titles use the main route automatically (CLIProxyAPI/luna). There
#   are no legacy AUX_PROVIDER/AUX_MODEL/AUX_BASE_URL title variables.
# - Long-context compression uses CLIProxyAPI Terra, then Luna. The plugin's
#   auxiliary guard refuses #privacy/#private payloads before cloud egress.
AUX_COMPRESSION_ROUTE=cliproxy
AUX_COMPRESSION_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra
AUX_COMPRESSION_FALLBACK_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# Where Hermes keeps everything: config.yaml, .env, honcho.json, SOUL.md,
# memories/, skills/, sessions, cron jobs, its venv and profiles/<name>.
# Default is ~/.hermes; set this only to put it somewhere else (all kit
# scripts and the systemd unit read it).
# HERMES_HOME=/home/you/.hermes
# Where profile book/notes corpora live, one folder per profile:
# $KNOWLEDGE_ROOT/<profile>/**/*.{md,txt}. `make hermes-profile NAME=<p>` copies
# that folder into the profile's knowledge/ (copy-only, additive, never deletes
# the source). Default data/knowledge; point at an SMB/CIFS mount to keep books
# off this host. Books are gitignored (data/); only the folder README is tracked.
# KNOWLEDGE_ROOT=/mnt/books/knowledge

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- Discord ---
# Bot token from https://discord.com/developers/applications (Bot -> Reset Token).
# Enable "Message Content Intent" and "Server Members Intent" on the bot.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
# Comma-separated Discord user ids allowed to talk to the bot (Developer Mode ->
# right-click your name -> Copy User ID). Leave empty = nobody (safe default).
DISCORD_ALLOWED_USERS=
# Channel id for proactive messages (cron results, kanban updates).
DISCORD_HOME_CHANNEL=
# Comma-separated channel ids where the bot answers without an @mention.
DISCORD_FREE_RESPONSE_CHANNELS=

# ------------------------------------------------------------- Browser Use ---
# Optional. Empty = Hermes drives a local Chromium through the Browser Use CLI.
# Set a key from https://browser-use.com to use Browser Use Cloud instead
# (managed Chromium, stealth, residential proxies).
BROWSER_USE_API_KEY=
